## 2. Who owns what

This workspace is generated from `firm/` by the design technology foundation.

| Location | Owner | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `firm/` | maintainers | Identity, tokens, logos, fonts. Change brand by editing these and re-rendering. |
| Files listed as `managed` in `.toolkit/manifest.json` | generator | **Do not edit.** Your edit becomes a conflict that blocks the next render. Change `firm/` or move the customization to a firm-owned file. |
| Files listed as `seed` | firm | Written once; edit freely. |
| Everything else | firm | Your tools and docs. The generator never touches them. |

Re-render with `python -m toolkit_cli render --workspace <this folder> --dry-run`
from a foundation checkout, read the plan, then run it without `--dry-run`.

## 3. Branches and contributions

- Branches are named `<human-owner>/<lowercase-task-slug>`, for example `{{ first_prefix }}/sheet-audit`. The prefix names the accountable human, even when an agent writes the code. AI or vendor prefixes (`claude/`, `codex/`, ...) are rejected.
- Never develop on `main`, `stable`, a detached HEAD, or another person's branch. Preserve work you did not create: never reset, clean, or move it to satisfy a check.
- Every change, including documentation, goes through a pull request. Passing checks do not authorize an agent to merge, release, or deploy; maintainers decide.
- Before editing, run `git status --short --branch` and `python validators/check_branch_policy.py`.

